Z||000000||fiero56||10-13-2001||06:45 PM||||Anyone using one? They look good, its a great idea. Wondering if anyone has had any problems with them, or any comments.<P>Rodney, if you read this, are there any issues with installing one on an '88? I think there were different CAT sizes over the years, not sure if there were or if it matters.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||10-13-2001||07:51 PM||||Call Rodney! He is very willing to help and is a great guy to talk too. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||XDrewX||10-13-2001||08:07 PM||||I just installed the cat I bought from Rodney.<BR>Believe it or not, it was the easiest thing I have ever done to my fiero, I just cut the old one out, installed the new one, intsalled the clamps, and I was done.<P>Rodney even supplies instructions on where to cut the old cat at and some tips for putting in the new.<P>I am very satisfied.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodney||10-13-2001||08:20 PM||||Rodney, if you read this, are there any issues with installing one on an '88? I think there were different CAT sizes over the years, not sure if there were or if it matters.<P>--------------------------------------------<P>I started by offering a few different lengths as I had some old converters from several years/engine sizes I had used to get the measurements from. I soon found that one size, 21 1/2" seems to fit all well and have had no complaints since going to this length. I found year and engine size was not always the same in relation to the lenght of the converter. I suspect different suppliers and variations in the welding set ups made the lengths vary some.<P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||MooCow||10-13-2001||10:45 PM||||I installed Rodney stright pipe and I love it.  It is pretty easy to do once you cut the cat out.  The picture instructions are easy too.  It makes the car have a meaner growl I love it.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||10
Z||000005||Sage||10-14-2001||12:03 AM||||Ah gee...I thought this post was gonna have a picture of Rodney's cat!  Meow?<P>(That's a joke son: sorry couldn't resist)<P>Have a good one!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||MrPBody||10-14-2001||12:17 AM||||I installed one on my '85 SE 2.5.  No problems, except exhaust work is always a pain in the neck.  Rodney's cat fits well, works great, and is very slightly louder than stock.  Sounds fine to me.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||10-14-2001||10:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MrPBody:<BR><B>I installed one on my '85 SE 2.5.  No problems, except exhaust work is always a pain in the neck.  Rodney's cat fits well, works great, and is very slightly louder than stock.  Sounds fine to me.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So the tighter you twist the tail, the louder the growl?||||reg||1
